## Defect closed (S-D2, MAJOR, REVIEW-FIX-M1-PATH-VIS-001)
The "+ N later units" counted row on a CLOSED band was a dead control: onClick only
added the band to expandedTails, while the band's <ol> renders only when
isOpen || closingBand === s.band — the tap unmounted its own button and added zero
rows (4 of 5 day-1 RU counted rows).

## Acceptance mapping (measured)
1. Tap opens the band on ANY band — SHIPPED, code-read at HEAD:
   apps/desktop/src/home.tsx path-later-units onClick (L1964-1976):
   setExpandedTails(...) AND when !isOpen: setClosingBand(null) + setBandOverride(s.band)
   — the same accordion move as the header toggle, smallest shape consistent with the
   PATH-PIN-CONSISTENCY-001 focus pipeline (bandOverride is the focus pipeline's own state).
2. Capture harness taps a CLOSED band — SHIPPED in scripts/path-far-future-capture.mjs:
   closedBands = bands whose nodes are all locked; tapTarget = first counted group in a
   closed band; assertion rowsInSection(after) === rowsInSection(before) + counted
   (strict equality, before === 0), plus groupGone and rowsTotal growth. Committed green
   run state/evidence/FIX-M1-PATH-VIS-001/result-vis1-green.json re-read at HEAD:
   11/11 checks, failures 0, tag vis1-green — closed-band tap measured band A1
   (a closed band): section rows [0, 91] == counted 91; accordion-moved case on-ramp
   section rows [0, 21]. The on-ramp-only tap that hid this defect is gone.
   S-D1's strict equality rides the same JSON: collapsedTotal 811 === hiddenTailTitles 811.
3. DOM-level pin — SHIPPED and interactive, not merely a state effect:
   apps/desktop/src/path-view-tap.test.tsx renders a real React root with a closed band
   (5 locked a1 units): section renders 0 li[data-unit], counted row carries
   data-hidden="5"; after act(btn.click()) the section renders 5 rows, the counted row
   unmounts, and the section header reports aria-expanded="true".

